// `npm run typecheck` = `tsc -p jsconfig.json --noEmit`. JSDoc-only: this
// project has no .ts files and no TypeScript syntax in .js (see AGENTS.md).
//
// checkJs is on for every file under src/. Files that are not clean yet open
// with `// @ts-nocheck — checkJs backlog` — that comment *is* the backlog
// (`grep -rl "@ts-nocheck" src`). To burn one down, delete the line, fix the
// real errors (narrow, add a JSDoc type, add a guard — not `@type {any}`), and
// keep `npm run typecheck` green. Never add @ts-nocheck to a file that passes.
//
// Mixins: both renderers attach most methods with applyXMethods(Klass) from
// other files, which tsc cannot see on the class. So:
//   - src/brain-renderer-webgl/*.js type their method literals with
//     `@satisfies {WebGLMixin}` (src/brain-renderer-webgl/types.js): `this` is
//     the whole renderer, and facade methods get the contract's signature.
//   - Do NOT put `@implements BrainRendererFacade` on either class expecting
//     tsc to see mixin methods — it can't. `npm run check:facade`
//     (scripts/check-renderer-facade.mjs) is the cross-file "does each backend
//     implement every facade method" check; do not delete it in favour of tsc.
//
// TypeScript 7 defaults to `strict`; noImplicitAny stays off so an untyped
// parameter is `any` rather than an error. That is deliberate, not a TODO.
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "Bundler",
    "allowJs": true,
    "checkJs": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "noImplicitAny": false,
    "lib": ["ES2022", "DOM"],
    "types": ["@webgpu/types"]
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*.js"],
  // src/shaders/** and src/ui/templates/** are checked too: they are plain
  // template-string modules and pass as-is. (`exclude` would only drop them as
  // roots — the renderers import the shaders, so they'd be checked anyway.)
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "dist"]
}
